STCropRotation = 369;					: farmer generates +1 food, gain food equal 50% of overfarming value :
STFertilizer = 370;						: each city generate +50% food after overfarming penalty :
STConcrete = 371;						: building cost 20% cheaper :
STStandardization = 372;				: building cost 10% cheaper, unit cost 10% cheaper, +10% Trade bonus :
STAdvancedMining = 373;					: double bonus from Iron, coal, gold, and silver :
STIndustrialization = 374;				: +10% Production output for each trade and production buildings :
STPrintingPress = 375;					: each research building generate +2 research :
STMeritBureaucracy = 376;				: Reduces corruption penalty by 20% :
STXenopsychology = 377;					: -3 unrest for each non-religious unrest reduction building, regular unit gains +1 resistance :
STScientificProcess = 378;				: each city get 25% research bonus :
STRadio = 379;							: Reduces corruption penalty cap to 20%, +20% Trade bonus, in combat regular units gain +10% To-Hit, +10% To-Defend, +1 Resistance :
STCorperateCharter = 380;				: +1/2/3% trade bonus in the city for each Marketplace/Bank/Merchants' Guild wizard control :
STSanitationReform = 381;				: +40 population growth of both city and outpost :
STNursingAndSurgery = 382;				: +40 population growth of both city and outpost, all regular units gain healer perk :
STStrategicLogistic = 383;				: All city get bonus from resource as if has half resouce tile in that city if one of the city own by the wizard access to that resource :
STObsolescenceRearmament = 384;			: All unit get equipment upgrade at the end of turn :
STHeatPowerEngine = 385;				: Each base production buildings gain +6 Production and increase by 50% if city has access to coal, all new mechanical unit gain power engine enchantment, power engine units movement increased by 1 :
STExplosive = 386;						: double miner guild output, +2 range attack and x2 fire breath for blackpowder unit, all melee/flying regular/mechanical units and humanoid summons get Thrown equal 10-max figure and wall crasher :
STBallisticsTraining = 387;				: in combat, all regular and humanoid summons non-magic range units gains +20 Range To-Hit :
STConscription = 388;					: Unit recruitment cost -20% :
STMilitaryDrilling = 389;				: All new regular units gain permanent Discipline enchantment :
STRocketry = 390;						: All new viable units gain Blackpowder upgrade :
STArmorClad = 391;						: all new mechanical units get armor clad permanent enchantment, +6 armor and +6 resistance :

STMagitekMagicalPhysics = 392;			: Fire/Lightning/Cold/Poison/Non-magic direct damage spell deal additional non-magical damage at 50% of their strength on its primary target :
STMagitekTechnoGeomancy = 393;			: Double casting skill output from Monument, Linking Tower, and Amplifying Tower :
STMagitekMaterialScience = 394;			: double output of ore that generate power, armorclad and battle armor unit gains free permanent resist magic :
STMagitekPowerEngine = 395;				: City generate power equal to 10% of production in the city. In combat, power engine units movement increased by 2, gains large shield, and +20% To-Defend :

STMagitekXenoveterinary = 396;			: In combat, fantastic creatures doped with +10% To-Hit, +25% HP. Armorclad upgrade apply to summon creatures too if has Obsolescence Rearm. requires 2 nature books :
STMagitekAntiGravityDrive = 397;		: All mechanical sailing units gain flying and stealth, in combat, mechanical sailing unit lose sailing, requires 2 sorcery books :
STMagitekBeamWeapon = 398;				: In combat, all regular units melee attack becomes Doom damage, requires 2 chaos books :
STMagitekPsycheForceConverter = 399;	: in combat, regular units gains To-Hit and To-Defend for each point of equal to Resistance x unit veterancy level, requires 2 Life books :
STMagitekPneumaReactor = 400;			: All regular units -Resistance/2 strength Life Steal, requires 2 Death books  :


